# The browser bundle is a build artefact committed inside the crate that embeds
# it, so that a consumer depending on the crate alone gets a working UI. Pin it
# to LF so a checkout does not rewrite it and make every rebuild look like a
# change.
assets/index.html text eol=lf

# The example's tables are written by the editor whenever it is developed
# against, and the editor writes LF. Pin them for the same reason.
examples/library/Data/*.jsonl text eol=lf

# The bundle is built from these sources and the page it builds is committed,
# so the build must not vary with the platform it ran on. A source checked out
# with CRLF carries those line endings into the page—Vite copies the body of
# index.html through verbatim—and the committed page then differs from the one
# CI builds. Pin them to LF so every checkout builds the same bytes.
Web/** text eol=lf
